<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Physician writing"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-568"}>{"Papers "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-569"}>{"Support "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Send the case "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-568"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"}>{"Case report"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/original-research-article/"}>{"Original research article"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-manuscripts/"}>{"Physician manuscripts"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/clinical-literature-review-for-an-evidence-based-medicine/"}>{"Clinical literature review"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-569"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/research-proposal/"}>{"Research proposal"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/literature-search-and-citation/"}>{"Literature search & citation"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/customized-writing/"}>{"Customized writing"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-training/"}>{"Physician training"}</a> </div> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Original Research Article Writing Service"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Original Research Article Writing Services"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"An original research article is not a write-up of what you did. It is a document a reviewer reads against a checklist, in the order that checklist is arranged, looking for the specific items that let them judge whether your finding is believable — and the study design decides which checklist. Pubrica’s research paper writing services turn clinical, experimental and observational data into publication-ready manuscripts for physicians, surgeons, academics and industry scientists — medical manuscript writing for randomized and non-randomised designs alike, written to CONSORT, STROBE, STARD, PRISMA, CARE or ARRIVE as the design requires, formatted to your target journal, and compliant with ICMJE and GCP throughout."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Send your data or your draft"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-or"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-or"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"One manuscript at a glance"}</b>{" · a cohort study"}</span> <span>{"STROBE · 3,500 words"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Reporting guideline chosen from the design, not by habit"}</b><span>{"STROBE"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Every checklist item present and locatable"}</b><span>{"22 of 22"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Unadjusted and adjusted estimates both reported"}</b><span>{"Both"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Confounder selection stated, not implied"}</b><span>{"Explained"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Formatted, referenced and checked for originality"}</b><span>{"Reports issued"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Data"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" framework "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" draft "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" stats "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" review "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"submission"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every manuscript"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Written to its reporting guideline"}</li> <li>{"Structured in IMRaD"}</li> <li>{"Checked for originality"}</li> <li>{"Formatted to the journal"}</li> <li>{"Authorship declared"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"From $300"}</b><span>{"Manuscript drafting, in 10–12 business days"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Supporting researchers through publication"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ICMJE · GCP"}</b><span>{"CONSORT, STROBE, STARD, PRISMA, CARE, ARRIVE"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <nav className={"pagenav is-scroll"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-what-we-do-3yaclq"} aria-current={"true"}>{"What we do"}</a><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-who-we-serve-1b141kc"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-our-compliance-12g304p"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-how-it-works-nvl4tm"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-our-experts-6o4wsb"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-sample-work-1u879zb"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-packages-1nrmyu2"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-guarantee-183r77f"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-client-stories-1wlqhz2"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-original-research-article-faq-1bneznt"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-what-we-do-3yaclq"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we do"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Seven pieces of work, and each can be commissioned on its own."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Our scientific manuscript writing service is offered in parts, because papers arrive at every stage — some as a spreadsheet and an idea, some as a draft an editor has already returned once. Empirical research of any design is covered by the same research manuscript writing process."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Clinical research design and protocol development"}</b> <span>{"The hypothesis framed so it can be tested, the variables chosen and operationalised, the endpoints defined, and the protocol written to GCP and ICH guidance — for studies not yet run, or for a protocol that has to be turned into something publishable. Our clinical research paper writing service carries the protocol through into the manuscript rather than rewriting it from scratch later."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Literature review and gap analysis"}</b> <span>{"The intensive review that defines what a high-impact paper is arguing against. The gap established by naming the specific deficiencies — in data type, sample size, population studied and geographic representation — so that a reviewer can check the claim rather than accept it, which is what separates a demonstrated gap from an asserted one."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Full manuscript writing and structuring"}</b> <span>{"Complete original research articles in IMRaD, written to the reporting guideline the design requires and to the structure your target journal uses — whether that is a general medical journal, a specialty title or a society publication. Tables and figures built as part of the draft, and the abstract written last, from the paper, rather than first from the intention."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Biostatistics and data interpretation"}</b> <span>{"Analysis in SPSS, R, STATA, SAS or NVivo, for clinical endpoints, patient-reported outcomes, survival data and qualitative observations. The model matched to the design, assumptions checked, effect sizes reported with confidence intervals, and a clear separation between what was pre-specified and what was exploratory."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Ethics documentation and regulatory compliance"}</b> <span>{"The ethics statement, the consent description, the registration entry and the declarations, written to what the journal will actually ask for. Support with institutional review board (IRB) submissions and with trial registration on ClinicalTrials.gov, CTRI or the registry your region requires — before the first participant, because afterwards the date is visible and permanent."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Journal formatting and submission support"}</b> <span>{"Formatting to the target journal’s author guidelines and citation style, references verified against the sources rather than matched to the citations, an originality and plagiarism check with correction, a cover letter that says why this journal, and the portal submission itself with every declaration completed."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Post-submission and revision support"}</b> <span>{"Reviewer comments triaged into what to concede, what to answer and what to decline with reasons; the revision made with tracked changes; and a point-by-point response letter cross-referenced to page and line. Where a paper is rejected, an honest view on whether to revise and resubmit, redirect to another journal, or stop."}</span> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Additions, quoted alongside"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Graphical and visual abstracts built from the finding rather than decorated around it; figures redrawn to journal specification in vector format; reference reformatting compatible with Zotero and EndNote; proofreading by native-speaker editors with a doctorate in the field; conversion of a thesis or dissertation chapter into an article, which is a genuine rewrite rather than a trim; reformatting for resubmission elsewhere; translation; and infographics. Each is quoted alongside a writing project rather than instead of one, because a graphical abstract of a paper that does not exist yet is a design exercise."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Article types we write"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Fifteen kinds of paper, and what each one has to prove."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Across clinical medicine, surgery, public health, pharmaceutical research and the laboratory — each with its own reporting guideline and its own way of being sent back."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Randomised controlled trials"}</b><span>{"Phase I to IV, written to CONSORT 2025 with the extension your design needs — and with allocation concealment, blinding and the flow diagram treated as load-bearing rather than as formalities."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Prospective and retrospective cohort studies"}</b><span>{"Cohort manuscript development to STROBE, with both unadjusted and adjusted estimates reported and the selection of confounders explained rather than implied."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Case-control and cross-sectional studies"}</b><span>{"Also to STROBE, with the matching described, the source of controls justified, and the direction of any plausible selection bias stated rather than acknowledged in general terms."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Diagnostic accuracy studies"}</b><span>{"To STARD, with the reference standard named and justified, the flow of participants shown, blinding between index test and reference stated, and the two-by-two counts given rather than only the summary measures."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Treatment outcome and comparative effectiveness"}</b><span>{"Where randomisation was not possible: the comparison groups defined, the confounding addressed by design where it could be, and the causal language kept in proportion to what the design supports."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Clinical audits and case series"}</b><span>{"Structured so that the standard audited against is explicit and the sample is described in full — the two things that separate an audit worth publishing from a description of local practice."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Case reports"}</b><span>{"To CARE, with the timeline, the differential diagnosis and what was ruled out, and written informed consent from the patient, which almost every journal requires and which is not optional."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Surgical innovation and technique comparison"}</b><span>{"Surgical outcomes work: perioperative outcome analysis, minimally invasive procedure reports and postoperative complication studies — with the learning curve addressed, because a reviewer who operates will ask about it."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Systematic reviews and meta-analysis"}</b><span>{"To PRISMA 2020, registered on PROSPERO before screening, with the search reproducible as written, risk of bias assessed with a named tool and certainty assessed with GRADE."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Epidemiological and public health studies"}</b><span>{"Disease surveillance, community health assessments, behavioural risk factor surveys and cross-national comparisons, with the sampling frame described and the response rate reported."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Health policy and health services research"}</b><span>{"Policy impact evaluations and services research, frequently non-randomised, reported to TREND where the intervention is behavioural or a public health programme."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Real-world evidence and pharmacoepidemiology"}</b><span>{"Studies from registries, claims and electronic health records, reported to STROBE with the RECORD extension, with the data provenance and the validity of the coded outcomes addressed directly."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Pharmacoeconomic and outcomes research"}</b><span>{"Cost-effectiveness and economic evaluation alongside clinical outcomes, with the perspective, the time horizon and the discounting stated, because a reader cannot interpret the result without them."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Post-marketing surveillance and pharmacovigilance"}</b><span>{"Safety studies and drug safety reporting, written for the journal audience rather than lifted from the regulatory document, which is a different register with a different reader."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Basic, translational and preclinical research"}</b><span>{"Laboratory and in vivo studies to ARRIVE 2.0, with randomisation, blinded assessment, a justified sample size and pre-set exclusion criteria — the four things that most improve preclinical reproducibility."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"And the fields they are written in"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Manuscripts are written by people qualified in the field they concern, across oncology, cardiology, neurology and psychiatry, endocrinology and diabetes, gastroenterology and hepatology, nephrology, respiratory and critical care, infectious disease and vaccines, immunology and rheumatology, dermatology, ophthalmology, urology, obstetrics and gynaecology, paediatrics and neonatology, geriatrics, anaesthesia and pain medicine, emergency medicine, general and specialist surgery, orthopaedics, radiology and imaging, pathology and laboratory medicine, rare and genetic disease, nutrition and dietetics, dentistry, nursing and allied health, public health and epidemiology, health policy, medical education, and medical devices and digital health. Where a study sits between two fields, two people are assigned rather than one stretched."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-who-we-serve-1b141kc"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who commissions a manuscript."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six kinds of author involved in evidence-based investigation, with the same underlying request: turn this study into a paper a reviewer can judge."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Physicians and clinicians"}</b><span>{"Practising doctors running clinical audits, case series and trials alongside a full clinical load — who need the writing handled without losing control of the clinical judgement in it."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Surgeons and procedural specialists"}</b><span>{"Surgical innovation, perioperative outcomes, technique comparison and complication analysis, written by people who know that a reviewer who operates will ask about the learning curve."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Academic researchers and faculty"}</b><span>{"Investigator-initiated and institution-based studies, basic and translational work, and mixed-methods research — written for the Scopus and PubMed-indexed journals a department is measured by, and for an examiner where the work is a thesis."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Postgraduate and doctoral candidates"}</b><span>{"Converting a thesis chapter into an article, which is a genuine rewrite rather than a trim, written to university guidelines and journal standards at the same time."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Pharmaceutical, biotech and industry scientists"}</b><span>{"Efficacy studies, bioequivalence work, real-world evidence and post-marketing surveillance, with patent-sensitive content handled carefully and the regulatory and journal registers kept apart."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Public health and epidemiology researchers"}</b><span>{"Community surveys, surveillance studies, behavioural research and patient-centred outcomes, with the sampling frame described and the response rate reported rather than omitted."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"The three moments people call"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"The best one is when the data is complete and nothing has been drafted. The framework can then be built properly, the reporting guideline chosen from the design, and the claim audit done before anybody has become attached to a sentence. The second is with a draft in hand, which is where most manuscripts arrive and is entirely workable — though the work usually turns out to be structural rather than linguistic, and a paper that needs its claims rewritten is not a paper that needs proofreading. The third is after a rejection, which is a better moment than it feels: a reviewer’s report is the only direct evidence you will ever get of how this literature reads your work, and it is worth an hour with somebody who reads them regularly before deciding whether to revise, redirect or stop. What nobody can do is turn an underpowered study into a convincing one, and where that is the situation we will say so rather than write around it."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-our-compliance-12g304p"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and guideline standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The standards a manuscript is held to."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Pubrica works in compliance with this guidance. The reporting guideline is chosen from the study design before any drafting starts, because it decides the structure — and a manuscript restructured afterwards reads like one."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"ICMJE recommendations"}>{"ICMJE"}<em>{"authorship · ethics"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ICMJE recommendations "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(authorship, disclosure and trust)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The four authorship criteria and the declarations that follow from them: contributions, funding, competing interests, data sharing, and the statement about any writing assistance. Prospective trial registration is a condition of consideration at every member journal, and retrospective registration is visible in the registry and permanent. Duplicate and redundant publication and undisclosed overlap with your own earlier work are the integrity findings that surface most often at submission."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--consort"} role={"img"} aria-label={"CONSORT and SPIRIT reporting guidelines"} /></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"CONSORT and SPIRIT "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(trials and trial protocols)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"CONSORT 2025 for the finished trial report and SPIRIT for the protocol, deliberately aligned so a protocol written to one already contains what the other will ask for. Extensions cover the design you actually ran: cluster, crossover, stepped-wedge, non-inferiority and equivalence, pilot and feasibility, N-of-1, patient-reported outcomes, harms, and AI-enabled interventions. The completed checklist is a submitted item at most journals."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"STROBE, STARD and PRISMA reporting guidelines"}>{"STROBE"}<em>{"STARD · PRISMA"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Guidelines for the other designs "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(STROBE, STARD, PRISMA, CARE, ARRIVE, TREND)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"STROBE for cohort, case-control and cross-sectional studies, with RECORD where the data was routinely collected. STARD for diagnostic accuracy, and TRIPOD+AI where the index test is a model. PRISMA 2020 for systematic reviews, with PRISMA-S for the search. CARE for case reports, ARRIVE 2.0 for animal work, and TREND for non-randomised evaluations of behavioural and public health interventions. The EQUATOR Network holds the current version of each, and the current version is the one that applies."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Declaration of Helsinki and Good Clinical Practice"}>{"HELSINKI"}<em>{"ICH-GCP"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Ethics and the conduct behind the paper "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(Declaration of Helsinki, ICH-GCP)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The Declaration of Helsinki governs research involving human participants and is what a journal’s ethics statement refers to; ICH-GCP governs how a clinical trial was run and what its documentation has to contain. Ethics committee approval with the reference number, the consent process as it actually happened, and registration before the first participant are all checked at submission rather than assumed, and a gap in any of them is found by an editor rather than a reviewer."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"COPE guidance on publication ethics"}>{"COPE"}<em>{"integrity · flowcharts"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Publication ethics in practice "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(COPE)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"COPE’s flowcharts are what an editor follows when something is questioned — an authorship dispute, suspected redundant publication, an image or statistical concern, an undisclosed conflict. Knowing what those processes look like is most useful before submission, because almost all of them are avoidable by settling authorship in writing at the start, disclosing overlap rather than hoping, and making sure every listed author has actually seen the final version."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Authorship, settled at the start"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"The ICMJE criteria are cumulative: substantial contribution to conception, design, acquisition or analysis; drafting or critical revision; final approval; and agreement to be accountable for the work. All four, not one. In practice the disputes arrive at submission and concern people added for seniority, people dropped after moving institution, or an order nobody wrote down — and by then there is a manuscript and a grievance rather than a conversation. We ask who the authors are and in what order in the first meeting, put it in writing, and revisit it if contributions change. Professional writing support is explicitly permitted by the ICMJE and explicitly required to be disclosed: where a Pubrica writer contributes substantially they are named in the acknowledgements with the funding source stated, and where the contribution meets the authorship criteria we say so and let you decide."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The author is you. That is not a formality."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Journals do not prohibit AI assistance; they prohibit undisclosed assistance, and none of them accept a tool as an author. Everything that reaches your manuscript has been read and verified by a person who can defend it to a reviewer."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Finding source material. Checking references against the papers they cite. Consistency of terms, figures and cross-references. Structural suggestions a writer accepts or rejects."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Generating claims the data does not support; drafting a discussion without the results in front of a human; inventing or reformatting references without verification; and any submission without the declaration the journal asks for."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as a research integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-how-it-works-nvl4tm"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How our research paper writing service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Our step-by-step process."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Seven stages, collaborative throughout — a subject-matter expert with clinical or academic expertise in your field, a statistician where the analysis needs one, and a project associate who owns the deadline."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage one"}</span> <h3>{"Consultation and assignment"}</h3> <p><b>{"A project associate and a subject-matter expert."}</b>{" The research question, the design, the data you have, the target journal and the audience — then a writer assigned by clinical or academic field rather than by availability. This is also where the reporting guideline is settled, because it is decided by the design and it decides the structure."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage two"}</span> <h3>{"The framework, agreed before drafting"}</h3> <p><b>{"The writer and you."}</b>{" An annotated outline: background, objectives, hypotheses and methodology, with every section mapped to the checklist item it answers and to the source the content will come from. You sign it off before any prose exists, because moving a section in an outline takes a minute and moving it in a finished manuscript breaks every cross-reference and every figure callout."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage three"}</span> <h3>{"Literature synthesis and the gap"}</h3> <p><b>{"Subject specialists."}</b>{" What has already been published, what it establishes, and what it leaves open — with the gap stated so a reviewer can verify it rather than take it on trust. The specific deficiencies worth naming are the ones in data type, sample size, population and geographic representation, because those are the gaps a new study can actually close."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage four"}</span> <h3>{"Drafting, section by section"}</h3> <p><b>{"The writer."}</b>{" Abstract, introduction, methods, results and the discussion section written to the journal’s structure and to the reporting guideline, with the methods written at the level that lets somebody repeat the study rather than at the level that summarises it. Tables and figures built as part of the draft rather than added to it, because the figure usually changes what the results paragraph should say."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage five"}</span> <h3>{"Statistical analysis, where you need it"}</h3> <p><b>{"Statisticians."}</b>{" Descriptive and inferential analysis in SPSS, R, STATA, SAS or NVivo for qualitative work, with the model matched to the design and the assumptions checked rather than assumed. Effect sizes with confidence intervals rather than p-values alone, and a clear statement of what was pre-specified and what was exploratory."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stages six and seven"}</span> <h3>{"Review, editing and submission"}</h3> <p><b>{"An independent reviewer, then the project associate."}</b>{" Your feedback incorporated, then language editing, reference verification against the sources, an originality check, and formatting to the journal’s author guidelines and citation style. Then the cover letter, the declarations and the portal submission — and when reviewer comments arrive, the point-by-point response."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} style={{ borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)", background: "var(--paper-2)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send the data. We will tell you what paper it makes."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Before anything is quoted, a subject-matter expert reads what you have and tells you which reporting guideline governs it, what the data can claim, and which journals publish work of this design and size. Two business days, at no cost. Sometimes the answer is that the dataset makes a stronger short report than a weak full paper — which is worth hearing before four months of drafting."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The field"}</b><span>{"Clinical research, surgery, public health, biotech"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The region"}</b><span>{"UK, US, EU, GCC, India, Asia-Pacific"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The audience"}</b><span>{"A named journal, or the kind you are aiming at"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The study"}</b><span>{"Design, data, protocol, and the ethics approval"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Any draft"}</b><span>{"A part-written paper, or a thesis chapter"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The rules"}</b><span>{"Journal, institutional or supervisor guidelines"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"If the paper has been rejected before, send the reviewer comments. They are the most valuable thing you can give us and the thing authors most often withhold, usually because reading them again is unpleasant. A resubmission that does not visibly answer them tends to collect the same criticism from a different reviewer."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"The skeleton"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Your design picks the checklist. Your word limit divides the paper."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Choose the study type and set the journal’s word limit. The manuscript apportions itself across IMRaD, each section shows the checklist items it is responsible for, and each shows the thing authors cut first when they run out of words — which is reliably the thing a reviewer looks for first."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"imr rv rv-d1"} data-imr={""}> <div className={"imr__bar"}> <span><b>{"Pick the design, then the word limit."}</b>{" Everything else follows from those two."}</span> <span data-imr-frame={""}>{"CONSORT · 20 items across four sections"}</span> </div> <div className={"imr__ctl"}> <div> <p className={"imr__k"}>{"What kind of study is it?"}</p> <div className={"imr__types"} role={"group"} aria-label={"Study type"} data-imr-types={""}><button type={"button"} className={"imr__t"} data-t={"0"} aria-pressed={"true"}><b>{"Randomised trial"}</b><span>{"CONSORT"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"imr__t"} data-t={"1"} aria-pressed={"false"}><b>{"Observational study"}</b><span>{"STROBE"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"imr__t"} data-t={"2"} aria-pressed={"false"}><b>{"Diagnostic accuracy"}</b><span>{"STARD"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"imr__t"} data-t={"3"} aria-pressed={"false"}><b>{"Systematic review"}</b><span>{"PRISMA"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"imr__t"} data-t={"4"} aria-pressed={"false"}><b>{"Case report"}</b><span>{"CARE"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"imr__t"} data-t={"5"} aria-pressed={"false"}><b>{"Animal research"}</b><span>{"ARRIVE"}</span></button></div> </div> <div className={"imr__wrap"}> <p className={"imr__k"}>{"The journal’s word limit"}</p> <input className={"imr__range"} id={"imr-range"} type={"range"} min={1500} max={6000} step={250} value={"3500"} aria-label={"Word limit for the manuscript body"} data-imr-range={""} /> <p className={"imr__wv"} data-imr-wv={""}><b>{"3,500"}</b><span>{"words for the body, abstract and references excluded"}</span></p> <p className={"imr__hint"}>{"Most clinical journals sit between 3,000 and 4,000 words for the body. Check your target journal before writing to any figure here, including this one."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"imr__gl"} data-imr-gl={""}><p className={"imr__glk"}>{"The guideline that governs it"}</p><p className={"imr__glt"}><b>{"CONSORT 2025"}</b>{", with the extension for your design — cluster, crossover, stepped-wedge, non-inferiority, pilot and feasibility, or AI-enabled intervention. "}<b>{"SPIRIT"}</b>{" governs the protocol the paper reports, and prospective registration is a condition of consideration at every ICMJE member journal. A completed checklist is a submitted item at most journals, and filling it in honestly is what surfaces the missing methods detail before a reviewer does."}</p></div> <div className={"imr__secs"} data-imr-secs={""}><div className={"imr__s"}><div className={"imr__sh"}><span className={"imr__sn"}>{"14% of the body"}</span><p className={"imr__st"}>{"Introduction"}</p><span className={"imr__sw"}>{"~490 words"}</span></div><div className={"imr__track"}><div className={"imr__fill"} style={{ '--w': "46.66666666666667%" }} /></div><div className={"imr__sb"}><p>{"Why this question, and why now. The shortest section in almost every manuscript, and the one authors overwrite."}</p><ul className={"imr__items"}><li>{"Scientific background and the rationale for the comparison"}</li><li>{"Specific objectives or pre-specified hypotheses"}</li></ul><div className={"imr__cut"}><i>{"First thing cut"}</i><span>{"The third paragraph of background. Reviewers do not need the field explained; they need the gap this trial closes."}</span></div></div></div><div className={"imr__s"}><div className={"imr__sh"}><span className={"imr__sn"}>{"30% of the body"}</span><p className={"imr__st"}>{"Methods"}</p><span className={"imr__sw"}>{"~1,050 words"}</span></div><div className={"imr__track"}><div className={"imr__fill"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div><div className={"imr__sb"}><p>{"Enough for somebody else to do it again. This is where the reporting guideline puts most of its weight, and where a methods reviewer spends their time."}</p><ul className={"imr__items"}><li>{"Trial design, allocation ratio, and any changes after it started"}</li><li>{"Eligibility criteria, and the settings and locations of the data"}</li><li>{"Interventions for each group in enough detail to replicate"}</li><li>{"Primary and secondary outcomes, defined and with any changes flagged"}</li><li>{"How the sample size was determined, and any interim analyses"}</li><li>{"Sequence generation, allocation concealment, and who did each"}</li><li>{"Who was blinded, and how"}</li><li>{"Statistical methods for primary and secondary outcomes, and for subgroups"}</li></ul><div className={"imr__cut"}><i>{"First thing cut"}</i><span>{"Allocation concealment and who was blinded. These are two lines, they are the two lines a methods reviewer looks for first, and they are routinely the two that go."}</span></div></div></div><div className={"imr__s"}><div className={"imr__sh"}><span className={"imr__sn"}>{"26% of the body"}</span><p className={"imr__st"}>{"Results"}</p><span className={"imr__sw"}>{"~910 words"}</span></div><div className={"imr__track"}><div className={"imr__fill"} style={{ '--w': "86.66666666666667%" }} /></div><div className={"imr__sb"}><p>{"What happened, with numbers and without interpretation. Every outcome you said you would report, including the ones that did not go your way."}</p><ul className={"imr__items"}><li>{"A flow diagram: randomised, received intervention, analysed, with losses"}</li><li>{"Dates of recruitment and follow-up, and why the trial ended"}</li><li>{"A table of baseline characteristics by group"}</li><li>{"Numbers analysed in each group, and whether by original assignment"}</li><li>{"For each outcome, the effect size with its precision"}</li><li>{"All harms in each group, with the same care as the benefits"}</li></ul><div className={"imr__cut"}><i>{"First thing cut"}</i><span>{"The harms table, moved to a supplement. CONSORT asks for harms in the results, and a paper that reports benefits fully and harms briefly is telling a reviewer something."}</span></div></div></div><div className={"imr__s"}><div className={"imr__sh"}><span className={"imr__sn"}>{"30% of the body"}</span><p className={"imr__st"}>{"Discussion"}</p><span className={"imr__sw"}>{"~1,050 words"}</span></div><div className={"imr__track"}><div className={"imr__fill"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div><div className={"imr__sb"}><p>{"What it means, what it does not mean, and what is wrong with it. Interpretation belongs here and nowhere earlier."}</p><ul className={"imr__items"}><li>{"Limitations, naming the sources of potential bias and imprecision"}</li><li>{"Generalisability to the population you actually studied"}</li><li>{"Interpretation consistent with the results, balanced against other evidence"}</li><li>{"Registration number, protocol availability, and funding"}</li></ul><div className={"imr__cut"}><i>{"First thing cut"}</i><span>{"The limitations paragraph, reduced to a generic sentence. Naming your actual weaknesses is more persuasive than hiding them, because the reviewer will find them either way."}</span></div></div></div></div> <p className={"imr__foot"}><b>{"The percentages are a working allocation rather than a rule, and the checklist items are summarised from the published guidelines rather than quoted from them."}</b>{" Use the full checklist from the EQUATOR Network when you write, and use your journal’s own author guidelines over anything on this page — word limits, structure and reference styles are set by the journal and vary widely. Guidelines are also revised: CONSORT was updated in 2025 and PRISMA in 2020, and the version that applies is the one current when you submit."}</p> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why the word limit is a scientific decision"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Every author who has fought a word limit has made the same trade in the same order: the methods lose their detail first, because the methods feel like the part the reader already understands. What actually goes is allocation concealment, who was blinded, how confounders were chosen, the interval between index test and reference standard — one line each, all of them invisible to the author and all of them the first thing a methods reviewer looks for. The result is a paper that reads well and cannot be judged, which is the most common reason a technically sound study is sent back for major revision. The way out is not writing shorter methods. It is writing a shorter introduction and moving the material a reviewer needs into the supplement with a pointer, rather than deleting it."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-our-experts-6o4wsb"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, the handover says which of them did which stage, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Question, scope, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, PRISMA"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"RoB 2, ROBINS-I, QUADAS-3, JBI"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, CONSORT"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible, so a reviewer, an editor or an assessor can run it again."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-sample-work-1u879zb"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What the framework contains."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"The first deliverable on any manuscript is not prose. It is the outline, agreed before drafting, and the audit of what your data can actually claim — which is the part clients do not know to ask for and the part that changes the reviewer’s report. Use the tabs to see each part."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Manuscript framework and claim audit"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"Retrospective cohort · 4,218 patients · STROBE · 3,500 words"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"The annotated outline · the claim audit · the analysis as planned · journal fit"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the manuscript framework"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"or-t1"} aria-controls={"or-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"The outline"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"or-t2"} aria-controls={"or-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"Claim audit"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"or-t3"} aria-controls={"or-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"Analysis"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"or-t4"} aria-controls={"or-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"Journal fit"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"or-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"or-t1"}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Introduction · ~490 words"}</dt><dd>{"Background and rationale, then the objective as a testable question. Two paragraphs, not four."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Methods · ~1,050 words"}</dt><dd>{"Design, setting, participants, variables, data sources, bias, study size, statistics. Where STROBE puts most of its weight."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Results · ~980 words"}</dt><dd>{"Flow, baseline table, events, unadjusted and adjusted estimates, subgroups, sensitivity. Every number traced to the analysis output."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Discussion · ~980 words"}</dt><dd>{"Key results, limitations with the direction of each bias named, interpretation proportionate to the design."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Outside the body count"}</dt><dd>{"Structured abstract to the journal’s headings, 4 tables, 2 figures, up to 40 references, declarations."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Every section mapped"}</dt><dd>{"To the checklist item it answers and the source its content comes from"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Signed off before drafting"}</dt><dd>{"Moving a section here takes a minute; moving it later breaks every cross-reference"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The one non-negotiable"}</dt><dd>{"The methods budget. A manuscript that loses its methods detail becomes impossible to judge."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"or-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"or-t2"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“X reduces the risk of Y by 34%”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Two problems in seven words. “Reduces” is causal and this is an observational cohort; and 34% is a relative reduction from an adjusted hazard ratio, which most readers will take as absolute. Rewritten as: X was associated with a lower rate of Y (adjusted HR 0.66, 95% CI 0.54 to 0.81)."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“Our findings demonstrate that earlier initiation improves outcomes”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Both verbs assert causation, and initiation timing is confounded by indication in a way that adjustment cannot remove. Rewritten to state the association and name the confounding explicitly."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“X should be considered for routine use”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"A practice recommendation from a single observational cohort. Rewritten as: these findings support evaluation of X in a randomised trial. This is the sentence authors resist most and the one reviewers object to most."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“Particularly strong in patients over 65 (p=0.03)”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"A within-subgroup p-value is not evidence that the effect differs by subgroup. The interaction test is, and it gives p=0.21. Rewritten to report both strata with the interaction p-value, labelled exploratory."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“No significant difference in the secondary outcome”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"The estimate is HR 0.91, 95% CI 0.72 to 1.15 — an interval containing both a 28% reduction and a 15% increase. Rewritten to give the estimate and say the study could not exclude a clinically important effect either way."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"5 of 6 claims rewritten"}</span><span>{"None of them because the science was weak"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"or-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"or-t3"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Design"}</dt><dd>{"Retrospective cohort, single health system, 2018 to 2024"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Participants"}</dt><dd>{"4,218 after exclusions, from 5,106 screened"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Events"}</dt><dd>{"512 primary outcome events; median follow-up 3.4 years"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Primary analysis"}</dt><dd>{"Cox proportional hazards, adjusted for the pre-specified confounder set"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Confounder selection"}</dt><dd>{"From a causal diagram agreed before analysis, not by stepwise selection — and said so in the methods"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Assumption check"}</dt><dd>{"Schoenfeld residuals; no proportional hazards violation for the primary exposure"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Missing data"}</dt><dd>{"6.2% on at least one covariate; multiple imputation with a complete-case sensitivity analysis"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Subgroups"}</dt><dd>{"Age, sex, baseline severity — tested by interaction, reported as exploratory"}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"or-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"or-t4"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Design and size fit the shortlist"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Three comparable cohorts have appeared in the shortlisted specialty titles in the past two years, so the design and scale are within what these journals publish."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The word limit is workable"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"3,500 words fits the allocation, provided the introduction stays at two paragraphs and the extended methods go to a supplement with a pointer rather than being deleted."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The abstract uses the journal’s own headings"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Which differ from the generic ones, and using the wrong set is a common desk-rejection trigger that costs nothing to avoid."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"What will be challenged"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Confounding by indication, the exploratory subgroup, and the single-system setting. All three are addressed in the discussion in advance rather than left for the response letter."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Fit argued from what these journals publish"}</span><span>{"Objections answered before they are made"}</span></p> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · author and study details changed"}</span><span data-docpage={""}>{"Page 1 of 4"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"The framework is the plan and the honest read of what the data supports. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each part."}</b></p> <p><b>{"The claim audit is the tab worth reading."}</b>{" Five of the six claims in the author’s draft needed rewriting, and not one of them because the science was weak. The study was sound. What the draft did was describe an association in the grammar of an experiment — which is the commonest reason an observational paper is returned, and which is fixable in the words rather than in the data."}</p> <p><b>{"Two of those rewrites are ones authors resist."}</b>{" Replacing “should be considered for routine use” with “supports evaluation in a randomised trial” feels like giving something up. It is the sentence that stops a reviewer deciding the authors have over-read their own data, and everything after it is then read more generously."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Structure agreed before any prose"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Every section mapped to its checklist item and its source."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Every claim checked against the design"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"With the rewrite supplied, not just the objection."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"The methods budget protected"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Because that is what a methods reviewer reads first."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Objections answered in advance"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"In the discussion, rather than in a response letter."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a framework built round a study like yours — same design, same field, same target journal."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-or"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-or"}>{"Read the full framework"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-or"}> <span><b>{"Read the full framework"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — the outline, the claim audit, the analysis and the journal fit"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-or"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Original research article · sample framework"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Manuscript framework and claim audit"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"Retrospective cohort study · 4,218 patients · STROBE · the annotated outline agreed before drafting, and every claim in the draft checked against what the design can support. Author, institution and study details have been removed or changed. Ask us and we will send one built around a study like yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"The framework, agreed before drafting"}</h4> <p>{"The first deliverable on any manuscript is not prose. It is an outline in which every section is mapped to the checklist item it answers and to the source its content will come from, signed off before a word is written. Moving a section here takes a minute; moving it in a finished manuscript breaks every cross-reference and every figure callout."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Section"}</th><th>{"What goes in it, and where it comes from"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Introduction"}<br /><i>{"~490 words"}</i></td><td>{"Background and rationale, then the objective stated as a testable question. Source: the literature synthesis, section 3 of the search report. Two paragraphs, not four."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Methods"}<br /><i>{"~1,050 words"}</i></td><td>{"Design, setting, participants, variables, data sources, bias, study size, statistical methods. Source: the protocol and the data dictionary. This is where STROBE puts most of its weight and where the word budget has to survive."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Results"}<br /><i>{"~980 words"}</i></td><td>{"Participant flow, baseline table, event counts, unadjusted and adjusted estimates, subgroup and sensitivity analyses. Source: the analysis output, with each number traced to a table in it."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Discussion"}<br /><i>{"~980 words"}</i></td><td>{"Key results, limitations with the direction of each bias named, interpretation proportionate to the design, generalisability. Source: this document, section 2."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Fixed elements"}</td><td>{"Structured abstract to the journal’s headings, 4 tables, 2 figures, up to 40 references, and the declarations. Outside the body word count."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Target journal body limit 3,500 words. The allocation above is a working plan rather than a rule, and the one part of it that is not negotiable is the methods: a manuscript that loses its methods detail to a word limit becomes impossible to judge, which is the commonest reason a sound study is returned for major revision."}</p> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"Claim audit"}</h4> <p>{"Every claim in the author’s draft, checked against what a retrospective cohort can actually support. This is the section clients do not know to ask for, and it is the one that changes the reviewer’s report."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Claim in the draft"}</th><th>{"Verdict"}</th><th>{"What the design supports, and the rewrite"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"“X reduces the risk of Y by 34%.”"}</td><td><b>{"Not supported"}</b></td><td>{"Two problems in seven words. “Reduces” is causal and this is an observational cohort; and 34% is a relative reduction derived from an adjusted hazard ratio, which most readers will take as absolute. "}<i>{"Rewrite: “X was associated with a lower rate of Y (adjusted HR 0.66, 95% CI 0.54 to 0.81).”"}</i></td></tr> <tr><td>{"“Our findings demonstrate that earlier initiation improves outcomes.”"}</td><td><b>{"Not supported"}</b></td><td>{"“Demonstrate” and “improves” both assert causation, and initiation timing is confounded by indication in a way adjustment cannot remove. "}<i>{"Rewrite: “Earlier initiation was associated with better outcomes, although confounding by indication cannot be excluded.”"}</i></td></tr> <tr><td>{"“X should be considered for routine use.”"}</td><td><b>{"Not supported"}</b></td><td>{"A practice recommendation from a single observational cohort. "}<i>{"Rewrite: “These findings support evaluation of X in a randomised trial.”"}</i>{" This is the sentence authors resist most and the one reviewers object to most."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“The effect was particularly strong in patients over 65 (p=0.03).”"}</td><td><b>{"Overstated"}</b></td><td>{"A within-subgroup p-value is not evidence that the effect differs by subgroup; the interaction test is, and it gives p=0.21. "}<i>{"Rewrite: report both strata (over 65: HR 0.55, 0.38 to 0.79; 65 and under: HR 0.74, 0.57 to 0.96) with the interaction p-value, labelled exploratory."}</i></td></tr> <tr><td>{"“No significant difference was found in the secondary outcome.”"}</td><td><b>{"Misleading"}</b></td><td>{"The estimate is HR 0.91 with a 95% CI of 0.72 to 1.15 — an interval that includes both a 28% reduction and a 15% increase. "}<i>{"Rewrite: give the estimate and the interval, and say the study could not exclude a clinically important effect in either direction."}</i></td></tr> <tr><td>{"“This is the largest cohort reported to date.”"}</td><td><b>{"Supported, with a caveat"}</b></td><td>{"True as of the search date, and it will not stay true. "}<i>{"Rewrite: “the largest cohort reported at the time of writing”, with the search date given."}</i></td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__cl"}><b>{"Five of six claims needed rewriting, and none of them because the science was weak."}</b>{" The study is sound. What the draft did was describe an association in the grammar of an experiment, which is the single most common reason an observational paper is returned — and it is entirely fixable in the words rather than in the data."}</p> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"The analysis, as planned"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Element"}</th><th>{"Value"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Design"}</td><td>{"Retrospective cohort, single health system, 2018 to 2024"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Participants"}</td><td>{"4,218 after exclusions, from 5,106 screened"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Events"}</td><td>{"512 primary outcome events; median follow-up 3.4 years"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Primary analysis"}</td><td>{"Cox proportional hazards, adjusted for the pre-specified confounder set"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Confounder selection"}</td><td>{"From a directed acyclic graph agreed before analysis, not by stepwise selection — and stated as such in the methods"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Proportional hazards"}</td><td>{"Checked on Schoenfeld residuals; no violation for the primary exposure"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Missing data"}</td><td>{"6.2% on at least one covariate; multiple imputation, with a complete-case sensitivity analysis"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Pre-specified subgroups"}</td><td>{"Age, sex, baseline severity — tested by interaction, reported as exploratory"}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Stating that confounders were chosen from a causal diagram agreed in advance, rather than by a stepwise procedure on the data, is two lines in the methods and it answers the question a statistical reviewer of an observational paper asks first."}</p> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"Journal fit"}</h4> <ul> <li><b>{"Design and size are appropriate"}</b>{" for a specialty journal publishing observational work of this scale; three comparable cohorts have appeared in the shortlisted titles in the past two years."}</li> <li><b>{"The 3,500-word limit is workable"}</b>{" with the allocation in section 1, provided the introduction stays at two paragraphs and the extended methods go to a supplement with a pointer rather than being cut."}</li> <li><b>{"The structured abstract"}</b>{" uses the journal’s own headings, which differ from the generic ones and are a common desk-rejection trigger."}</li> <li><b>{"What will be challenged:"}</b>{" confounding by indication, the exploratory subgroup, and the single-system setting. All three are addressed in the discussion in advance rather than left for the response letter."}</li> </ul> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"What is handed over"}</h4> <ul> <li>{"The annotated framework, with every section mapped to its checklist item and its source."}</li> <li>{"The claim audit, with each claim, its verdict and the rewritten sentence."}</li> <li>{"The completed STROBE checklist, with the page and line for every item."}</li> <li>{"The full manuscript in the journal’s format, with tables, figures and the structured abstract."}</li> <li>{"A verified reference list, checked against the sources rather than matched to the citations."}</li> <li>{"The originality report, and the cover letter."}</li> <li>{"The declarations: ethics approval with its reference, consent, funding, competing interests, data availability and the writing assistance statement."}</li> </ul> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Pubrica supports the manuscript; the science, the claims and the authorship remain yours, and the paper is submitted in your name. Professional writing assistance is permitted by the ICMJE and required to be disclosed: where a writer contributes substantially they are named in the acknowledgements with the funding source stated, and where the contribution meets the authorship criteria we say so and let you decide. Any AI assistance in drafting is declared."}</p> <div className={"fsm__end"}> <p>{"Prepared by Pubrica. Pubrica is a trading name of Guires"}<sup className={"reg"}>{"®"}</sup>{", registered in England, Wales and India."}</p> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/downloads/pubrica-original-research-article-sample.pdf"} download={""}>{"Download this as a PDF"}</a> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"ba rv"}> <div className={"ba__hd"}><span><b>{"Before and after"}</b>{" · one sentence from a results section, redacted"}</span><span>{"Randomised trial · CONSORT 2025"}</span></div> <div className={"ba__g"}> <div className={"ba__c ba__c--b"}> <p className={"ba__k"}>{"As it arrived"}</p> <p className={"ba__t"}>{"Treatment significantly reduced pain scores compared to control (p = 0.03), demonstrating the efficacy of the intervention."}</p> <ul className={"ba__f"}><li><span>{"Interpretation in the Results section, where the reader expects findings and nothing else."}</span></li><li><span>{"No effect size and no confidence interval, so the reader cannot judge whether the difference matters."}</span></li><li><span>{"“Demonstrating efficacy” from a single p-value of 0.03, which is a claim the data cannot carry."}</span></li><li><span>{"No baseline and no units, so the reduction could be enormous or trivial."}</span></li></ul> </div> <div className={"ba__c ba__c--a"}> <p className={"ba__k"}>{"As it went out"}</p> <p className={"ba__t"}>{"Mean pain score at 12 weeks was 3.1 (SD 1.8) in the treatment group and 4.4 (SD 2.0) in the control group, a difference of 1.3 points on the 0–10 numerical rating scale (95% CI 0.4 to 2.2; p = 0.03). The minimum clinically important difference for this scale is 2 points."}</p> <ul className={"ba__f"}><li><span>{"The estimate is reported in the units the outcome was measured in."}</span></li><li><span>{"The interval is given, and it is what tells the reader the effect could be smaller than it looks."}</span></li><li><span>{"The clinically important difference is stated, which is what turns a number into a finding."}</span></li><li><span>{"The interpretation moves to the Discussion, where a reviewer expects to argue with it."}</span></li></ul> </div> </div> <p className={"ba__foot"}><b>{"The confidence interval here runs from 0.4 to 2.2 points against a clinically important difference of 2."}</b>{" The trial is compatible with a benefit patients would not notice. That belongs in the Discussion, stated plainly — and a paper that states it is far harder to reject than one that hopes nobody checks."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What a Pubrica manuscript delivers"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What it gives you."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A paper a reviewer can judge, and claims you can defend at every stage after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"bens rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"01"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Written to the checklist that will be applied"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The reporting guideline chosen from the design before drafting, and every item present and locatable — because journals increasingly require the completed checklist with page numbers, and filling one in honestly is what surfaces the missing methods detail before a reviewer does."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"02"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Claims proportionate to the design"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Association described as association, subgroups reported with their interaction tests, a null result given with its confidence interval rather than as an absence of difference. Over-reading your own data is the fastest way to have a sound study returned, and it is entirely fixable in the words."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"03"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The methods a reviewer needs, kept"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Allocation concealment, who was blinded, how confounders were chosen, the interval between index test and reference — one line each, the first things authors delete under a word limit, and the first things a methods reviewer looks for. We take the words from the introduction instead."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"04"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Your clinical time back"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"A full original research article takes a practising clinician somewhere between forty and eighty hours, spread across months of interrupted evenings. The parts only you can do — the question, the clinical judgement, the interpretation — are a small fraction of that."}</span></span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-packages-1nrmyu2"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three tiers, and everything can be adjusted."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Priced on study design, discipline, target journal and word count. Each is run by a writer qualified in your field, with a statistician drawn in where the analysis needs one and a project associate who owns the deadline."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Basic"}</span> <h3>{"Manuscript drafting"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Researchers early in a publishing career, whose data is complete and whose methodology is settled"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $300"}</b><span>{"quoted on the study, in 2 days"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"10–12 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Manuscript structured in IMRaD, with the framework agreed first"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Introduction, methods, results and discussion drafted in full"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Formatting to one target journal and its citation style"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Language editing to native-speaker level"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Originality check, with the report included"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: statistics; figures; response to reviewers."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-or"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-or"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Basic"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Advanced"}</span> <h3>{"Writing and compliance"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Researchers aiming at journals with strict reporting requirements"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $500"}</b><span>{"quoted on the study, in 2 days"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"12–15 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Basic"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Literature synthesis with the gap demonstrated, up to 25 references"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Statistical analysis in SPSS, R or STATA"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Tables, graphs and figures built to journal specification"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Methodology guidance, and hypothesis and objective refinement"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Completed checklist for CONSORT, STROBE, PRISMA or your design"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Ethics and competing interest statements, and two revision rounds"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: journal selection; submission; graphical abstract."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-or"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-or"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Advanced"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Premium"}</span> <h3>{"Submission-ready, end to end"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Researchers targeting indexed journals who want it handled through to a decision"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $750"}</b><span>{"quoted on the study, in 2 days"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"15–18 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Advanced"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Journal selection, with three titles and the reasoning for each"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Cover letter and the author response draft"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Formatting for more than one submission, in case of rejection"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Submission through the journal portal, with every declaration completed"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Unlimited revisions within scope, and one round of response to reviewers"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Further review rounds and resubmission elsewhere are quoted separately."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-or"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-or"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Premium"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "22px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"365 days of revision support, on every tier"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Revision support runs for a full year from delivery, on every package including Basic. Journals take months to respond and reviewers ask for things nobody anticipated, so support that expires in thirty days expires exactly when you need it. Inside that year, revisions within the agreed scope are included and uncapped: a reviewer asking for a reanalysis, a journal changing its format, a co-author joining late. What sits outside it is new work — a different study, a second paper from the same dataset, or a rewrite for a journal in another field — and we will say which side of the line something falls on before starting rather than after."}</p> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"Additions are quoted alongside any tier: statistical analysis or revalidation of an existing one; reference reformatting compatible with Zotero and EndNote; a graphical abstract or redrawn figures; proofreading by a native-speaker editor with a doctorate in the field; institutional review board documentation; conversion of a thesis chapter into an article, which is a rewrite rather than a trim; reformatting for resubmission to a different journal; translation; and a fast-track option where capacity allows, quoted on capacity rather than on urgency."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-guarantee-183r77f"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A manuscript can be excellent and still be rejected, because the decision belongs to an editor. Here are the terms before you commit to anything."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Revision until the manuscript meets the brief and the guideline it is written to, with no cap on rounds inside the scope agreed. A refund does not get your paper published; it leaves you with the same data and less time."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Unlimited revisions"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Inside the scope agreed, with no cap and no clock. A co-author joins late, a supervisor changes the framing, the target journal changes. We revise."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A guideline item missed, a reference wrong, a formatting rule misread — if it came from us, correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Delivered on the date agreed"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Conference deadlines and thesis submission dates do not move. If a date is genuinely at risk you hear it early with what can be done, not on the day."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Your paper stays yours"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"We draft, argue a view and tell you plainly when we disagree with a claim you want to make. What goes in your name is settled by you, every time."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" We cannot guarantee acceptance, and we will not quote an acceptance rate as though it were one — the decision belongs to an editor and a reviewer, and any supplier promising you publication is describing something they do not control. We will not write a claim the design does not support, however it is framed; where a draft needs one to work we will say so and offer the claim the data does support. We do not fabricate, adjust or selectively report data, and we do not remove an inconvenient finding. We will not write a paper for a journal that solicited you by email with a promise of rapid publication, and we will tell you why when we decline. And where the honest answer is that the dataset makes a stronger short report than a weak full paper, that is what you will hear."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"A subject expert reads it free"}</p> <p>{"Before anything is quoted, a Pubrica subject matter expert in your field reads what you have and tells you which reporting guideline governs it, what the data can claim and which journals publish work of this design and size. That conversation occasionally ends with us saying the study needs another analysis before it is writable — unwelcome in week one, and considerably better than at review."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Authorship settled at the start"}</p> <p>{"Who the authors are and in what order, agreed in writing at the first meeting against the ICMJE criteria and revisited if contributions change. Almost every authorship dispute we see arrived because nobody wrote it down, and by the time it surfaces there is a manuscript and a grievance rather than a conversation."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"GDPR, patient data and confidentiality"}</p> <p>{"A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves, and writers and project staff are bound by internal confidentiality agreements as well. Unpublished data is held under GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, kept only as long as the project needs it, never used to train anything and never shared outside your project team. Where a dataset contains patient identifiers we ask you to remove them before sending rather than removing them ourselves, because de-identification is a decision your ethics approval governs."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Declared, not ghosted"}</p> <p>{"Professional writing assistance is explicitly permitted by the ICMJE and explicitly required to be disclosed, and the disclosure is what makes it legitimate. Where a Pubrica writer contributes substantially they are named in the acknowledgements with the funding source stated; where the contribution meets the authorship criteria we say so and let you decide. That is the opposite of ghostwriting rather than a polite version of it. Any use of AI in drafting is declared to you, and we follow whatever your target journal requires about it."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-client-stories-1wlqhz2"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three manuscripts, and what changed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named researcher has confirmed it in writing."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Client testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“They went through our cross-sectional study line by line against the STROBE items and found four we had simply not addressed. Two of them were single sentences.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"PUBLIC HEALTH"}<br />{"RESEARCH"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Cross-sectional"}<br />{"Study"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Dr Anitha Raj"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Assistant professor · India"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"JIF —"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“The most useful part was being told which of our sentences claimed more than the design could support. We would have argued about it with a reviewer instead.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--c"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"TRANSLATIONAL"}<br />{"MEDICINE"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Cohort"}<br />{"Study"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Prof. Markus Klein"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Biomedical researcher · Germany"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"JIF —"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“Structuring the oncology manuscript to CONSORT from the outline stage rather than at write-up is what made the peer review straightforward.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"ONCOLOGY"}<br />{"RESEARCH"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Randomised"}<br />{"Trial"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Dr Sanjay Menon"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Clinical oncologist · India"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"JIF —"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""}><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot is-on"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 1"} /><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 2"} /></div> <div className={"tcar__btns"}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-original-research-article-faq-1bneznt"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Original research article FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Ten questions authors ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure which reporting guideline governs your study, or whether your draft claims more than the design supports? "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-0"}><span>{"How can I structure an original research article for journal submission?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"In IMRaD — introduction, methods, results and discussion — with a structured abstract, keywords, references, tables and figures around it, and all of it to the journal’s own headings rather than generic ones. But the structure is the easy half. What actually decides whether the paper can be judged is the reporting guideline your design falls under, because that determines which specific items each section is responsible for: CONSORT for a randomised trial, STROBE for cohort, case-control and cross-sectional studies, STARD for diagnostic accuracy, PRISMA for a systematic review, CARE for a case report, ARRIVE for animal work, TREND for non-randomised intervention evaluations. Take the current checklist from the EQUATOR Network, write to it from the outline stage rather than checking against it at the end, and complete it honestly — the gaps it exposes are exactly the ones a reviewer will find."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-1"}><span>{"What are best practices for writing a clear and precise methodology section?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Write it so somebody else could repeat the study, which is a considerably higher bar than describing what you did. In order: the design named explicitly rather than left to be inferred; the setting, the dates and how participants were identified; eligibility criteria as they were actually applied; every variable defined, including the confounders and how they were chosen; the measurement methods and their comparability across groups; how the sample size was arrived at; the statistical methods with the model, the handling of missing data and which analyses were pre-specified; and the ethics approval with its reference number. Two things carry more weight than their length suggests. For a trial, allocation concealment and who was blinded — two lines that a methods reviewer looks for first. For an observational study, how the confounder set was selected: an adjusted estimate with an unexplained adjustment set is the commonest reason such a paper is sent back."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-2"}><span>{"How do I present statistical results effectively in my research article?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Lead with the effect size and its confidence interval, and treat the p-value as secondary. An interval tells a reader the range of effects your data is compatible with; a p-value on its own does not, and it is why “no significant difference” is so often misleading — a hazard ratio of 0.91 with an interval from 0.72 to 1.15 has not excluded a clinically important benefit or harm, and saying it found no difference misreports it. Report every outcome you said you would, including the ones that did not go your way. Give counts alongside percentages so a reader can recompute. Say which analyses were pre-specified and which were exploratory. For subgroups, report the interaction test rather than a p-value within each subgroup, because a difference between strata is what you are claiming and the within-stratum p-value is not evidence of it. And keep interpretation out of the results entirely — that is what the discussion is for, and a reviewer will say so."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-3"}><span>{"How can I write a compelling discussion and conclusion section?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Four moves, in order. State the key result in relation to the objective, once, without restating the results section. Put it alongside what is already known and say specifically where it agrees and disagrees rather than listing adjacent studies. Then the limitations — and this is where most discussions lose the reviewer, because a generic paragraph about sample size and single-centre design reads as a formality. Name your actual weaknesses, and for each one say which direction it would push the estimate. A reviewer who sees that you have understood your own study’s vulnerabilities reads everything else more generously. Finally the conclusion, proportionate to the design: an observational study supports the case for a trial, not a change in practice. That last sentence is the one authors resist most, and it is the one that stops a reviewer deciding you have over-read your own data."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-4"}><span>{"How do I ensure my article meets journal formatting and citation requirements?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Read the author guidelines for the specific journal, not the publisher’s general page, and read them before writing rather than after. What varies and matters: the word limit and whether it includes the abstract and references; the abstract’s required headings, which are journal-specific and using the wrong ones is a common desk rejection; the citation style, which in medicine is usually Vancouver as set out in the NLM and ICMJE recommendations, though AMA and APA appear too; limits on the number of tables, figures and references; figure format and resolution; and which declarations and statements are mandatory. Use a reference manager rather than formatting by hand, but check the output against the sources, because a manager reproduces whatever is in the record including its errors. Then complete the reporting checklist with page numbers, which most journals now ask for as a submitted item."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-5"}><span>{"What common mistakes should I avoid when preparing a research manuscript?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Eight, in roughly the order we find them. Causal language for an observational design — “reduces”, “improves”, “demonstrates” — which is the single most common problem and the most fixable. Methods too thin to judge, usually because they lost the word-limit fight to the introduction. Subgroup findings reported without an interaction test. A null result described as showing no difference, when the confidence interval says otherwise. Outcomes reported that differ from the ones registered or protocolled, which registries now make visible and reviewers now check. Conclusions that outrun the design. An introduction of four paragraphs where two would do. And the annexes left to the end: the ethics reference, the registration number, the declarations and the completed checklist, which is where submissions fail on the final afternoon. Six of the eight are decided before drafting starts."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-6"}><span>{"How can I respond effectively to peer review comments?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Triage every comment into one of three: concede and change; answer with evidence and change nothing; or decline with a reason. Most authors do the first two and avoid the third, which is a mistake — a reviewer who is wrong about something can be answered courteously, and editors expect it. Then write the response as a point-by-point letter, reproducing each comment and answering it directly underneath, with the page and line of every change so nobody has to hunt. Make the changes visible with tracked changes as well. Tone matters more than authors expect: reviewers are unpaid, they read your paper closely enough to find the problem, and a response that reads as irritated affects the editor’s decision. And answer every comment, including the ones you think are minor. An unanswered comment is the thing a reviewer notices on the second round."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-7"}><span>{"How can professional editing or support improve my research manuscript?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Mostly by reading it as a reviewer will rather than as its author does. The three things that change outcomes are structural rather than linguistic: checking every claim against what the design supports, which is where most sound studies lose credibility; working through the reporting checklist item by item to find the missing lines; and protecting the methods budget when the word limit bites. Language editing sits underneath all of that and matters for a different reason — a paper that is hard to read is read less carefully, and a reviewer who has to work to follow the argument attributes the difficulty to the science. What professional support does not do is improve the study. If the design cannot support the claim, better writing makes that clearer rather than less clear, and we would rather say so at the quote stage than at review."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-8"}><span>{"Which reporting guideline applies to my study, and where do I find it?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-8"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"The design decides it. Randomised trial: CONSORT 2025, with the extension matching your design — cluster, crossover, stepped-wedge, non-inferiority, pilot, N-of-1, patient-reported outcomes, harms, or AI-enabled intervention. Cohort, case-control or cross-sectional: STROBE, with RECORD if the data was routinely collected and STROBE-MR for Mendelian randomisation. Diagnostic or prognostic accuracy: STARD, with TRIPOD+AI where the index test is a model. Systematic review: PRISMA 2020, with PRISMA-S for the search and PRISMA-ScR for scoping reviews. Case report: CARE. Animal study: ARRIVE 2.0. Non-randomised evaluation of a behavioural or public health intervention: TREND. Qualitative research: COREQ or SRQR. The EQUATOR Network maintains all of them with their current versions, and current is the operative word — CONSORT was revised in 2025 and PRISMA in 2020, and writing to a superseded version is a visible error."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-9"}><span>{"Can you turn my thesis chapter into a journal article?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-9"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, and it is a rewrite rather than a trim, which is the part that surprises people. A thesis chapter is written to demonstrate competence to an examiner: the literature review is exhaustive because breadth is being assessed, the methods narrate what you learned as you went, and the discussion covers everything. A paper is written to convince a reviewer of one claim in three and a half thousand words, so the literature review becomes two paragraphs that establish a gap, the methods become a reproducible account with the false starts removed, and the discussion argues a single point. It is also common that one chapter contains two papers, or that two chapters make one — deciding that is the first conversation. Two practical points: check your university’s policy on publishing from a deposited thesis, since some repositories make the chapter publicly available and a journal may treat that as prior publication; and settle authorship with your supervisor in writing before drafting rather than after."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-10"}><span>{"How long should each section be?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-10"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"As a working proportion for a 3,500-word original article: introduction around 500 words, methods 800 to 1,000, results 800 to 1,000, discussion 900 to 1,200. The introduction is the section most often twice the length it should be, and the methods the section most often half. A useful discipline is that the introduction has three jobs and about four paragraphs in which to do them — what is known, what is not, and what this study did — and that anything else belongs in the discussion. The "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/free-tools/#submission-timeline"} data-nav={""}>{"submission timeline planner"}</a>{" and the manuscript skeleton on this page both work from the journal’s own limit rather than a generic one."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-11"}><span>{"Can you help choose the journal as well?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-11"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, and it is better done before the final draft than after. Journals differ in what they will consider, not only in what they will accept: a single-centre observational study, a null result, a study without a pre-registered protocol, or a device paper without a comparator each have a narrower set of realistic homes than the field as a whole. Deciding early means the paper is written to a real target — its structure, its word limit, its reporting checklist — rather than reformatted twice after the first two rejections. Our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/publication-support/journal-selection/"} data-nav={""}>{"journal selection service"}</a>{" does this from the manuscript rather than from a list."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-12"}><span>{"What do we do about an author who will not respond?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-12"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Deal with it before submission, because it becomes considerably harder afterwards. ICMJE requires every listed author to approve the final version and to agree to be accountable for it, and most journals now ask the corresponding author to confirm that in writing. A silent co-author is therefore a submission blocker rather than an inconvenience. In practice the routes are: a documented deadline with a clear statement of what will happen, a move to the acknowledgements if their contribution does not meet the authorship criteria, and — if it does and they cannot be reached — a conversation with the editor rather than a submission that misrepresents approval. Settling authorship in writing at the start prevents nearly all of this."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-13"}><span>{"How do we handle a result that contradicts our hypothesis?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-13"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Report it, in the section where results belong, with the same detail as a confirmatory one. A study that pre-specified an outcome and found no effect is a finding, and it is increasingly publishable — registered reports exist precisely to remove the incentive to bury it. What damages a paper is not the null result but the response to it: an outcome quietly swapped for one that worked, a subgroup promoted to the abstract, or a discussion that argues the study was underpowered without saying so in the limitations. The discussion should state what the confidence interval rules out, which is usually a more useful sentence than any claim the data could have supported."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-14"}><span>{"Our study is small and single-centre. Is it publishable?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-14"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Frequently, provided the paper claims what the design supports. A small single-centre study cannot establish generalisable effectiveness, and a discussion that implies it will draw the objection that sinks the paper. What it can do well is report a precise, well-characterised population, describe an effect with its interval, and say what a larger study would need to test. Journals that publish this kind of work exist and are identifiable in advance. The two things that decide the outcome are whether the reporting is complete against the relevant checklist and whether the limitations section names the real limitations rather than the conventional ones."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"or-15"}><span>{"Should my manuscript be in British or American English?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"or-15"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Follow the journal, and then be consistent, because a mixed manuscript is one of the first things a copy-editor flags. The pairs that matter most in research writing are randomisation and randomization, analyse and analyze, modelling and modeling, labelling and labeling, behaviour and behavior, centre and center, and programme and program — and most American journals want randomized controlled trial rather than randomised. Two traps a spell-checker will not catch. Oxford style uses -ize endings in British English, so "}<em>{"organize"}</em>{" and "}<em>{"summarize"}</em>{" are correct British spellings in some journals and wrong in others. And the spelling of a proper noun does not change: the World Health Organization keeps its z whichever variety you are writing in. We set the variety at the start from the target journal and apply it to the whole manuscript, including the figure labels and the supplementary files, which is where inconsistency usually survives."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of the manuscript."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A paper needs a study behind it and an editor in front of it, and both are work in their own right."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"BEFORE THE PAPER"}</b><em>{"the study it reports"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/experimental-design/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Experimental design"}</b><span>{"The study designed before it is run, so the paper has something to report."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/biostatistics-and-statistical-programming-services/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Biostatistics and statistical programming"}</b><span>{"The analysis behind the numbers, with the assumptions checked rather than assumed."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"ALONGSIDE IT"}</b><em>{"the evidence and the writing"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/literature-review-and-gap/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Literature review and gap analysis"}</b><span>{"The gap demonstrated so a reviewer can check it, rather than asserted."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Medical writing"}</b><span>{"The other documents the same study owes, each in its own register."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"GETTING IT ACCEPTED"}</b><em>{"the editor and the reviewer"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/journal-selection/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Journal selection"}</b><span>{"Which journals publish this design at this size, decided from the manuscript."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/peer-review-pre-submission/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Pre-submission peer review"}</b><span>{"The objection heard before an editor’s reviewer makes it."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading on structure and journals."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces from our library on how research is structured, placed and written."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"https://pubrica.com/academy/physician-writing/how-to-structure-case-reports-review-articles-journals/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How to structure case reports and review articles for medical journals"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Medical journals expect a set structure, with clear objectives and a reporting guideline behind each section."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-should-physicians-choose-the-right-journal-for-submitting-a-case-report/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How should physicians choose the right journal for submitting a case report?"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Publishing takes more than clinical knowledge; it demands a strategic read of which journals still publish what, and how."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-physicians-can-write-clear-and-impactful-patient-education-materials/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How physicians can write clear and impactful patient education materials"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Patient education materials carry health literacy. Clear ones change adherence; unclear ones quietly cost it."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send the data. A subject expert will read it before we quote."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Which reporting guideline governs it, what the data can claim, and which journals publish work of this design and size — in two business days, at no cost and with no obligation."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
